  "methodology": "Diagnostic wall/current-thread CPU intervals. Three native annotation loads per actual workspace during startup and original file selection. Complete original five payloads compared structurally with retained baseline JSON; the published record contains only their hashes. Both 4096-record native rings show no eviction. Observed semantic-worker names checked: atlas.compile, atlas.project.extract, atlas.search and analysis.render. Not a controlled latency improvement, field percentile, physical-input guarantee, atomic filesystem snapshot, new refinement, live-model/cold-install or confidentiality validation.",
  "ownership": "Production registers the existing Lean prepared-description reader. Additional reader dispatch and complete refusal use a second synthetic registration in unit tests; finite source preparation remains an existing independent real Z3 registration, not a new finite annotation reader.",
  "remaining": "Remove duplicated loader work without weakening original input/resource checks; bind observation revisions across concurrent capture; complete generic layout/source collection, native freshness waits, first-exposure rendering and the retirement audit under the full plan.",
